🐧 Linux Advanced – Real-World DevOps Scenarios
	1.	Load average is very high, but CPU usage is low. How do you troubleshoot?
	2.	System is slow even though CPU and memory look fine. Where do you investigate next?
	3.	A server is experiencing frequent OOM kills. How do you identify and fix the root cause?
	4.	Disk I/O wait is high. How do you diagnose storage performance issues?
	5.	Network latency is high between two Linux servers. How do you troubleshoot it?
	6.	A process intermittently spikes CPU and then disappears. How do you debug it?
	7.	How do you tune Linux kernel parameters for high-traffic applications?
	8.	A production system is running out of file descriptors. How do you fix and prevent it?
	9.	How do you investigate context switching and scheduler issues?
	10.	System time drift is causing application issues. How do you detect and fix it?
	11.	How do you analyze performance issues using strace, lsof, vmstat, iostat?
	12.	A server becomes unresponsive under load. How do you capture diagnostics safely?
	13.	How do you tune Linux for containerized workloads?
	14.	How do you analyze memory fragmentation and slab usage?
	15.	How do you prepare Linux systems for high availability and resilience?

